# Day Tripper, the ostinato riff (figure 4.1)
# Pollack types it on an eighth-note grid under the counts, so the rhythm is marked: E held three
# eighths, the D tied across the barline, the F# held two eighths. Fx is F double-sharp (the
# hammer-on to G#). Octaves follow the guitar/bass riff: up from low E to the E an octave above,
# dropping the octave when it repeats, as the essay notes.
# Register: sounding pitch, E2-E3; the F# in bar 2 leaps up a fifth from B2 to F#3 (checked by ear).
key E

system
words "Beats"  | 1*0.5 &*0.5 2*0.5 &*0.5 3*0.5 &*0.5 4*0.5 &*0.5 | 1*0.5 &*0.5 2*0.5 &*0.5 3*0.5 &*0.5 4*0.5 &*0.5 |
voice "Riff"   | E2*1.5 F##2*0.5 G#2*0.5 B2*0.5 E3*0.5 D3*0.5 | -*1 B2*0.5 F#3*1 B2*0.5 D3*0.5 E3*0.5 |
